INT. ORBITAL HYDROPONICS BAY, STATION KESTREL - CONTINUOUS

Racks of lettuce under violet light. Pipes sweat. A hum like a slow pulse. The floor is a grid, the ceiling a curve.

COMMANDER INGRID SORENSEN-AKINTOLA (50s, gray crop, crisp jumpsuit) walks the aisle with a tablet. Behind her trails botanist FELIX OYELARAN-DUBOIS (30s, goggles pushed up, hands green to the wrist). At a bench, engineer MARISOL TRAN (30s, ponytail, wrench in hand) tightens a valve. In the far corner, a robot technician, UNIT FOUR (a squat maintenance drone with a cheerful chirp), polishes a lens. The newest arrival is medic CASIMIR OKONKWO-BLYTHE (40s, trim beard), who leans in the hatchway.

INGRID
(to the bay)
Status report, everyone. Now.

FELIX
Lettuce is thriving.

MARISOL
Valve's holding.

UNIT FOUR
Beep. All systems nominal.

CASIMIR
Medically, I'm bored.

INGRID
That's what I like to hear.

A low metallic thud echoes from the water tank behind the racks. All five turn.

FELIX
That's not supposed to happen.

MARISOL
(muttering)
Of course it is.

Ingrid raises a hand. Silence. Another thud, closer. The lights dim a fraction. Unit Four chirps and rolls backward.

INGRID
Felix, Marisol, check the tank. Casimir, with me.

FELIX
^Yes, Commander.

MARISOL
^Yes, Commander.

They reply in unison and split. Felix and Marisol creep toward the tank. Ingrid and Casimir circle the racks opposite, tablet and medkit held like weapons.

Behind the tank, a fat grey cat, ORION, sits atop a coil of hose, licking one paw. It meows.

Everyone stops. Felix laughs first, a startled bark. Marisol sags against the rack. Ingrid pinches the bridge of her nose.

INGRID (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Who smuggled a cat onto my station?

Unit Four rolls up and nuzzles the cat's head with a mechanical arm.

UNIT FOUR
Beep. New crew member detected.
